well right now doctors from the clark  county medical society are gathering  virtually to talk about the vaccine  eight news now reporter kate houston  spoke to a local pulmonologist  about the vaccine and how it could  impact people who do have severe  allergies  as the nation continues to roll out the  covid19 vaccine  doctors are urging some groups of people  to take precautions  if they know they have a history of  anaphylactic reaction  they should be prepared local  pulmonologist dr evelyn montalvo stanton  says there have been some reported cases  of patients having an anaphylactic  reaction to the vaccine  for those with a history of severe  allergic reaction she recommends  bringing an epipen  benadryl or an inhaler it's very few  cases that we see so far but it's better  to be  cautious dr montalvo stanton says those  with a history of serious anaphylaxis  should get the vaccine in a controlled  environment they should make  an appointment with your specialist or  health care provider  and not have it done in these  pharmacy areas because there's no health  care  health care provider there that can help  you if you run into an anaphylactic  reaction  although many people do get seasonal  allergies especially in las vegas  dr montalvo stanton says this  recommendation is only for  severe cases if somebody has regular  allergies to an environment or certain  foods  and it's not as bad and have no problem  it's not an issue but  for those that have a history of severe  allergies  definitely they need to be prepared  those with a history of serious allergic  reactions  are encouraged to consult with their  doctor or specialist  kate houston 8 news now
 

